1
00:00:00,800 --> 00:00:04,492
Dr. Leila Shirazi checked
the signal three times.

2
00:00:04,532 --> 00:00:08,530
First she thought it was an
error, then interference.

3
00:00:08,570 --> 00:00:12,490
By the third check, she
couldn't deny it any longer.

4
00:00:12,530 --> 00:00:16,033
Five days after two
bunker-busters hit Fordow,

5
00:00:16,073 --> 00:00:19,422
the assessment had read
“fully neutralized.”

6
00:00:19,462 --> 00:00:24,192
But the signal held a regular
rhythm inside its irregularity —

7
00:00:24,232 --> 00:00:27,039
a truly dead system couldn't do that.

8
00:00:27,079 --> 00:00:29,248
She began writing the report.

9
00:00:29,288 --> 00:00:33,347
The last transmission from
a source codenamed ZARRIN,

10
00:00:33,387 --> 00:00:36,209
routed through the Islamabad channel,

11
00:00:36,249 --> 00:00:41,855
had arrived with seven coordinates for
a surviving sublevel and one line:

12
00:00:41,895 --> 00:00:44,330
“This is the last transmission.”

13
00:00:44,370 --> 00:00:47,072
The source's safety was in question.

14
00:00:47,112 --> 00:00:50,306
Seven months ago she'd written that only a

15
00:00:50,346 --> 00:00:54,080
kinetic intervention could
change the trajectory.

16
00:00:54,120 --> 00:00:56,365
They'd made that intervention.

17
00:00:56,405 --> 00:01:00,936
If it hadn't been enough — what
came next, she didn't write.

18
00:01:00,976 --> 00:01:02,423
Someone else would.
